      "body": "Queue task 3044 / issue #1153 — first slice per triage 2433: the shared framework core only. Per-provider adapters (#1159, #1161, #1163, #1165, #1301) are untouched and will consume this.\n\n## What this adds — `pm-stack/aggregator/src/token-adapter.ts`\nGeneralizes the meta-exporter as-built pattern (`pm-stack/meta-exporter/meta-quota-export.mjs`):\n\n- **Credential contract (references only, never values):** `CredentialRef` = a Bitwarden item name or a file path with a declared `0600` mode. `validateCredentialRef` rejects any object carrying a credential value (token/cookie/secret/… keys), a file ref without the 0600 contract, or an unknown kind. `credentialRefLabel` gives a log-safe label. No real credential is captured, stored, or logged by this slice.\n- **Session health check:** `classifyHttpProbe` — 401/403 or a redirect to an auth page = `expired`; 200 = `ok`; anything else = `unknown` (never silently either).\n- **Fail-closed client base:** `collectAdapter` runs fetch → session classification → parse. Parse drift raises `unparseable` and the **previous value is retained with its age** (`stale`, `ageSeconds`) — never zeroed. `session-expired` sets `needsRelogin` (the re-login/user-owned signal) and is structurally distinct from a genuine zero-usage reading, which is an `ok` outcome whose parsed value is 0. With no previous value, a failure yields `value: null` — never a fabricated reading.\n- **File-export adapter:** `collectFileExportAdapter` re-expresses the #1151 file-export source on the framework, reusing `entryFromFileExport` (the mapping is not rebuilt). One deliberate strictness divergence from the bare mapping: the mapping skips malformed windows, the adapter treats a success document with missing/malformed windows as **unparseable** and retains the previous entry. Producer-stale maps to `transport-unavailable` (unreachable, not zero).\n\n## Divergence note vs #1115 / the as-built exporter\n#1115 (managed-credential pattern design) is still open; this slice builds to the meta-exporter as-built pattern as triage directed. Divergences: classification lives at the collection layer as typed outcomes instead of per-exporter process exit codes, and the framework is TypeScript in the aggregator (where the quota-current consumers live) rather than a standalone .mjs per provider.\n\n## Tests\n`test/token-adapter.test.ts` — 13 tests: credential contract (value-carrying refs rejected, 0600 enforced), probe classification, drift→unparseable with previous retained + aged, expiry→re-login with previous retained, genuine zero ≠ expiry, transport failure with no previous → null, and the file-export adapter (healthy doc → entry labelled `file-export/meta-laptop`, expired doc, drifted doc, stale/missing doc).\nLaptop: `bun test test/token-adapter.test.ts test/quota-current.test.ts` — 26 pass. Files biome-formatted.\n\nRefs #1153\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/2115?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-light-v3.svg\"><img alt=\"View with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3-3x.png\" width=\"162\" height=\"28\"></picture></a> <a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1795841349&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=2115&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F2115&signature=1231314857f1c7c2d4f6081a4f2dda1dd22a00ba5cb7419c3616aa14cb759876\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup>Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added support for collecting usage data from browser tokens and file exports, including mapping valid file-export data to quota readings.\n  * Credential references are checked to ensure they use a supported format and do not contain embedded credential values.\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * When a refresh fails or data is unavailable or invalid, the last available reading is retained and its age and session status are reported. Expired sessions are flagged as requiring re-login.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
