      "body": "Fixes #944.\n\n## Problem\nThe markdown↔ProseMirror codec had no round-trip fixpoint for strong/em+link marks: `**[text](url)**` and `[**text**](url)` converted into each other on every save. The parse direction appends marks outermost-first (wrapper arms push as they nest, `convert_node`), while the save direction (`create_marked_text`/`build_mark_chain`) treated the marks array as innermost-first.\n\n## Fix (pkgs/id/src/web/markdown.rs only)\nOne canonical mark nesting order, outermost first — `link > strong > em > strikethrough > code` (`mark_nesting_rank`) — applied by **both** directions:\n- Parse: `text_node_with_marks` emits marks sorted into canonical order, so every spelling of the same marked text parses to the identical ProseMirror doc.\n- Save: `create_marked_text` sorts incoming marks (any array order, e.g. editor-produced) into canonical order before wrapping, so the same doc always saves to the same markdown: `[**text**](url)`.\n\n## Tests\nNew two-round-trip fixpoint tests in `web::markdown`: strong+link (both spellings + PM-doc convergence), em+link, strong+link with title (href/title survive), strikethrough+link, and the `***both***` bold-italic control. Local run status is reported on #944 by the queue worker; CI is the verifier of record for the full suite.\n\nQueue task 1091 (repo-health-code-pilot).\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/985?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-light-v3.svg\"><img alt=\"View with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3-3x.png\" width=\"162\" height=\"28\"></picture></a> <a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1795621534&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=985&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F985&signature=f24037611e845ac03047b657ac7317128f68c78684af9571b825ba9bd3de353b\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup>Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Markdown formatting now stays consistent when bold, italic, strikethrough, and links are combined, regardless of mark order. Link titles and repeated saves are also handled consistently.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
